course: dictionary
lesson: 7810
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word question can mean different things. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which one is right. «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying» uses question for something someone asks you, which you can answer or dodge.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «It's a question of time», question means a matter to think about or decide, not a sentence. «Out of the question» means impossible, and «without question» means for sure.
explain: Question is also a verb. To question someone is to ask them many things, like the police do. To question something is to doubt it. Read the words near the word, then ask: what would fit here?
fact: A question is a sentence that asks something.
fact: In maths, a question is a problem on a test or quiz.
fact: In science, a good investigation starts with a question.
fact: «Out of the question» means impossible. «Without question» means for sure.
fact: Respect means asking polite questions, not laughing at someone's food, clothes or customs.
exercise: «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying.» What does question mean here? | *Something someone asks you, which you answer | A problem on a test or quiz | Asking someone many things for a long time | A matter still to be decided
exercise: «It's a question of time.» In this sentence, question means: | To doubt something | A problem on a test | A sentence that asks something | *A matter to think about or decide
exercise: «Out of the question» means: | Outside, in the playground | Very easy | For sure | *Impossible
test: «Without question» means: | Maybe | Lost | *For sure | Angrily
test: When someone says «I question that story», they mean: | They have a test problem about it | They want to ask it many things | They are asking a sentence | *They doubt it
exam: In school, «put your hand up to ask a question» means question is: | To doubt something | A matter to decide | A problem on a test or quiz | *A sentence that asks something
